To run our model:
1. Install the required libraries (one time only). Open a terminal (macOS/Linux) or Command Prompt (Windows) and run:
pip install streamlit pandas scikit-learn

2. Download the project. Download the Veritas Final Version folder (or the .zip file) and unzip it. Check that it contains:
Veritas Final Version/
├── WiseLoanScript.py
└── Data/
    └── credit_risk_dataset.csv

3. Go to the project folder. It must contain both the script and the Data folder:
Veritas Final Version/
├── WiseLoanScript.py
└── Data/
    └── credit_risk_dataset.csv
Example: if you unzipped it into Downloads:
cd ~/Downloads/"Veritas Final Version"
or you can just drag the Veritas Final Version folder from Finder/File Explorer into the terminal window and press Enter.

3. Start the app:
streamlit run WiseLoanScript.py
The app opens in your web browser automatically. If it doesn't, go to http://localhost:8501.

4. The first load takes a few seconds while the model trains. Then:
- Loan Prediction (sidebar): enter the applicant's details and press Predict Loan Risk.
- About: shows the three models compared and why Random Forest was chosen.
